WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.356
A bottle, a cap, an old phone.

00:00:03.356 --> 00:00:06.233
Recognizing them is only the beginning.

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:16.300
Circular OS connects visual evidence, human review, local
context, and clear actions, helping households and businesses
decide what to do next.

00:00:16.708 --> 00:00:22.111
Take or upload a photo, and review it before sending it to Meta.

00:00:22.111 --> 00:00:25.435
Then photograph another product or add another image.

00:00:25.435 --> 00:00:32.916
Earlier objects and corrections stay in the assessment, up to
eight objects, each linked to its own photo.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:39.863
Muse Spark proposes visible objects, materials, and condition,
and transcribes readable labels.

00:00:39.863 --> 00:00:44.217
Textiles, mixed products, and electronics have distinct
categories.

00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:54.556
These suggestions need review: an image cannot prove fibre
composition, weight, commercial value, or acceptance by a
recycling centre.

00:00:54.958 --> 00:01:02.261
Select Highlight object, and SAM three point one draws a box and
mask on the correct photo.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:06.557
Inspect the evidence, correct the classification, and confirm
your review.

00:01:06.557 --> 00:01:10.423
The original model proposal remains in the technical record.

00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:16.331
Choose household or business, and declare receiving channels you
have confirmed.

00:01:16.331 --> 00:01:19.330
Reuse and composting access also matter.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.829
Versioned rules produce reproducible recommendations.

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:24.827
Electronics stay on a specialist route.

00:01:24.827 --> 00:01:31.824
A district name never becomes an invented collection point or a
promise of acceptance.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.494
Larger controls and natural voice guidance make the steps easier
to follow.

00:01:37.494 --> 00:01:43.175
Enable audio preparation, and the next screen waits until its
guide is ready.

00:01:43.175 --> 00:01:46.671
Continue without audio, or press Play to listen.

00:01:46.671 --> 00:01:49.293
English and Spanish guidance are available.

00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:55.198
The plan explains what to do, why, and what still needs
checking.

00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:58.400
Pending reviews cannot masquerade as completed tasks.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:04.346
Download a readable PDF, print it, or export technical evidence
and policy details.

00:02:04.346 --> 00:02:08.006
A task checkmark is never proof of delivery.

00:02:08.417 --> 00:02:14.528
Our proposed free pilot starts in Lince, Lima, with older adults
in mind.

00:02:14.528 --> 00:02:19.229
The aim is participation and potential income through agreed
partners.

00:02:19.229 --> 00:02:23.929
Delivery, weighing, verified receipt, and recorded compensation
must come first.

00:02:23.929 --> 00:02:27.220
Partners and payments are not yet live.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:31.451
Future business services could support organizations that need
accountability.

00:02:31.875 --> 00:02:36.774
Circular OS turns identification into a reviewed, traceable next
step.

00:02:36.774 --> 00:02:45.101
Try the working demo at circular os dot circulapp dot L A, and
inspect the public source.

00:02:45.101 --> 00:02:47.061
Circular intelligence for everyone.

